claims.text:
Claim: box-constrained forward-model MLE in log k achieves validation rel_l2 in original k-space at most 0.9 times that of the fixed-configuration extra_trees control trained on 3000 raw rows.

Method: vectorised LM, 3 seeded starts, 40 iterations, authorized context.forward. The arm uses privileged access to the exact data-generating simulator (inverse crime). It uses training rows only for layout detection and a 20-row solver check.

Success: the 97.5th-percentile paired-bootstrap ratio (B=2000, seed 0) is below 0.9. All rows stay in the metric.

Uninformative if any of the following holds:
- C-Q1-6c fails;
- fidelity_pass is false or FORWARD_FIDELITY_REPORT is missing;
- solver_pass is false;
- layout_ok is false or the physics permutation disagrees with the fidelity ordering;
- timed_out is true;
- n_budget_fallback > 0;
- predict_calls != 1;
- the validation SSE median exceeds the chi2_76 median + 15;
- any gate report is missing or unparsable.

Scope: an upper bound under perfect specification against this specific untuned baseline, conditional on the seed-0 control. Seed-1 fragility is reported. Box asymmetry is stated: physics is clipped; extra_trees is inherently in range.

